From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:13:30 -0400
Subject: fix: the code review's filed items, and a tab group's header in the
 sidebar

The code review of 2026-10-15 (docs/history/review-2026-10-15.md) filed nine items it
could not fix the same hour, BACKLOG S-201 to S-209; the operator asked for them fixed too,
and for an unnamed tab group's blank header, seen in a test window, S-210.
One patch at the tip, as patch 0065: the fixes touch code of a dozen patches.

Routing. Only the tab a link from another app makes spends its mark: an address typed into
a fresh tab within the mark's ten seconds had taken it (routing D3). A Chrome shortcut file
opened from Finder is read first, and its target opens as any link from another app, small
or in the Space chosen for such links; the file's own address had been checked and marked
(routing D3, little E1). A host route takes an IPv6 literal and a port that is the scheme's
default; the pattern was cut at its first colon (routing D1).

Keyboard and screen readers. The welcome flow finds the focused control again by a key it
carries, so a label that changes or a block drawn above it no longer drops the focus, and a
control the redraw disables hands it to the next one; its three choice groups are named
(welcome W12). Clear is a focusable button named Clear, run by Enter, Space or a screen
reader's press; it was text painted on the line (spaces B17).

Data. A deleted Space's jar stays on the profile's pending list until its wipe has
finished, and the profile's next window finishes a wipe a quit cut short (sessions S17).
Undo brings a tab that was in no tab group back in none, so its folder comes back (tabs
R27). A new profile started after a profile move that could not happen makes a keychain key
of its own instead of copying Chromium's (windows N8).

Look. A Chromium tab group's header in the sidebar is a row like a folder's: a dot in the
group's colour, the title in the rows' text colour, an unnamed group's tab count muted for a
title, no fill but the hover tint. It was a bar filled with the group's colour, blank for
an unnamed group (folders F36; the operator's screenshot of a test window).

Tests. The Arc sidebar test checks that a copy was read; a wrong key unseals nothing; each
step of two browser scenarios stops only itself; the three upstream HTTPS-First tests the
series' default broke expect it, and the local startup histogram counts it as on.

Why: each item is behaviour its spec states, a privacy promise (a deleted Space's data), or
a test that could not fail.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next rebase folds each fix into the patch that owns
its code (patches/README.md, the round-patch exception).
