+// is all host ("::1"). A port matches the address's port, the scheme's
+// default included ("example.com:443" is "https://example.com/"). The rule
+// was cut at its first colon, so no IPv6 host matched, and a default port,
+// which the address does not spell, never did (BACKLOG S-203).
+bool HostRuleMatches(std::string_view pattern, const GURL& url) {
